have you ever wondered why extremely  rich people buy very expensive art  pieces  well there could be many reasons like  love for art status investment tax  saving etc  in this video let us throw some light on  how they can save taxes  we know that other assets like houses  have limitations in value or have  benchmarks  but in the case of paintings there is no  true valuation now what does that mean  this means they can pay any amount of  money for the paintings they wish to buy  let's understand this with an example  let's say a super rich person buys a  very rare painting worth 10 million  dollars from the auction market  one spot they generally do not hang them  at their homes or offices  they immediately transfer it to free  ports and store them there  wait what are free ports a free port is  a place where the normal tax system and  customs rules are not applicable it's  like a free trade zone now as long as  this painting is sold from these free  trade zones no taxes will be involved  fast forward let's say the painting is  now estimated to be worth 25 million  dollars the person will now simply  donate the painting to a museum and get  a tax write-off of 25 million dollars  because it is now considered to be  charity  so on the investment of 10 million  dollars the person saved 15 million  dollars in the form of taxes  amazing right did you know that in some  countries you can keep your expensive  paintings with you even if you go  bankrupt  read the first comment to know more
 

